# The factory's environment. Copy this to .env in the target repo's root.
#
# THIS ROSTER USES NO API KEYS.
#
# Every agent runs on `openai-codex/*`, which pi reaches through the Codex plan's
# OAuth — the same login you already use in the terminal. There is no
# OPENAI_API_KEY here, and there should not be: a key would charge per use while
# the plan is already paid for.
#
# Check with:  pi --list-models     (the `provider` column must say openai-codex)
# If the login expires, run `pi` and log in again — a key is not the fix.
#
# Switching provider later (anthropic, openrouter, fireworks) means coming back
# here and declaring THAT provider's key. Nothing validates this for you:
# `agents.validate()` only checks the provider/id format, not reachability.

# Optional overrides
# PI_PATH=pi                       # the pi binary, if it is not on PATH
# PI_MODELS_PATH=~/.pi/agent/models.json
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # your lane's label; defaults to git user.name
